    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Static Constants",
    "long_instructions": "## Create an App Shell\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Store the app's title and date in a local `appConfig` object and display them instantly. This creates a fast app shell so the user isn't staring at a blank screen while waiting for the internet.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\nAsk the AI to help you with each of these step-by-step.\r\n\r\n1. Create a `const` object named `appConfig`. Inside, add a `title` (text) and a `date` (text).\r\n\r\n2. Write a function named `renderAppShell`. Inside, update the display to use the title and date from your `appConfig` object.\r\n\r\n3. Call `renderAppShell()` at the bottom of your code so the text appears on the screen immediately.\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Show me how\r\n\r\n::: details [Step 1]\r\n*Drag out the instructions panel to enlarge the image*\r\n![](https://images.code.org/b8151205cf87db0bbad75ffc2d59fa70-image-1772822007248.png)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [Step 2]\r\n*Drag out the instructions panel to enlarge the image*\r\n\r\n![](https://images.code.org/446d0bab3ef1443fd0f020bab0db04bb-image-1772822074193.png)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [Step 3]\r\n*Drag out the instructions panel to enlarge the image*\r\n![](https://images.code.org/85aeef9f26e6e3a1f06213b25daf4872-image-1772822104628.png)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n",
